From: VDR-Suite S1 native SearchTimer preparation
Subject: [PATCH] epgsearch: serialize legacy search-rule writes under SearchExts owner lock
Upstream-base: 0118b4129c3601c04c7483f2fd04b604d4a2a980

The existing GetSearchFromID() returns a raw pointer after dropping its
inner lock. The service and SVDRP writers must hold the list owner's
outer mutex while selecting and mutating a rule. Likewise ID assignment
and insertion must be in the same critical section. The OSD on/off
assignment and Save() must remain atomic as one operation.

This patch is an isolated native prerequisite. It does NOT add a stable
per-rule generation, revision, native compare-and-swap, persistence/rollback,
or any Public API v1 write capability. Other OSD edit/delete and automatic
mutation pathways need the same end-to-end audit before native CAS ships.
It MUST NOT be used to authorize unsafe SearchTimer API mutations.

